.claude
issues.md
gui(abandoned)
webgui(abandoned)
*.bak
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Runtime artefacts — machine state and logs, not source.
error_log.txt
detector_status.ini

# THIS REMOTE IS PUBLIC. Everything below contains other people's data:
# fan display names, their messages, and purchase amounts. Screenshots of the
# live Infloww UI in particular show real handles in the tab strip and chat.
# The code needs none of it at runtime — only slice_elements.py and
# `automation.py --image` read these, and both are pointed at a file by hand.
#
# The listener itself is NOT in here: it is runtime, so it lives in automation/
# and is tracked. Only the screenshots and the one-off detector prototypes stay.
infloww ui elements/

# Screenshots automation.py drops while debugging a miss. Live UI, so same rule
# as above — the code recreates the folder on demand.
automation/debug/

# The USER's hotkeys. hotkeys.default.ini is what ships; HK_Init creates this from
# it on first run and merges in anything a later release adds, without touching a
# key that already has a value. Tracking it would put the maintainer's personal
# bindings into every fresh clone, and the updater used to overwrite everyone's.
hotkeys.ini

# Message content. Kept local; MMA regenerates it as you archive.
mass_archive.txt
